From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:33:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] state the crop region a centred camera applies

The camera service splits an application's zoom into CONTROL_ZOOM_RATIO and
a residual SCALER_CROP_REGION, sends both to the HAL, and joins them again
in the result: it unscales the result's crop region by the result's ratio.
The result stated the whole active array instead of the residual, so above
about 57x on a 4032 x 3024 array the region an application got back was
a pixel or three off (CTS testDigitalZoom on the front camera, which
checks the region within 5%).

The camera crops about the centre of the array only (CENTER_ONLY), so the
result now states the region it applies (camera_crop.hpp, the overlay's
rule): the requested size, centred in the active array of the sensor
mode in use, clamped to the array and to the smallest size the maximum
digital zoom allows. The session layer (ZoomRatioMapper) has already
divided the request's region by the zoom ratio when the camera sees it and
multiplies the result's region by the ratio afterwards, so in the camera's
space the zoom the service reports is the array over the region, and the
smallest region is the array over the maximum zoom, whatever the ratio. The
origin of the request is not used. A request with no region or an empty
one gets the array, as before. The host scales a frame to the stream's
size and applies the zoom ratio; the result's region is not a residual
crop of the picture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../hwl/EmulatedRequestState.cpp              | 20 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedRequestState.cpp b/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedRequestState.cpp
index 3884d28cd14f819fe8dafee44dd6424f1fbc4661..d214e7f5077a99d1fc1ddbc07b1cbac40b6bae0f 100644
--- a/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedRequestState.cpp
+++ b/devices/EmulatedCamera/hwl/EmulatedRequestState.cpp
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <utils/HWLUtils.h>
 
 #include "EmulatedRequestProcessor.h"
+#include "camera_crop.hpp"
 
 namespace android {
 
@@ -1200,8 +1201,23 @@ std::unique_ptr<HwlPipelineResult> EmulatedRequestState::InitializeResult(
     if (info.sensor_pixel_mode_ == ANDROID_SENSOR_PIXEL_MODE_MAXIMUM_RESOLUTION) {
       chosen_crop_region = info.scaler_crop_region_max_resolution_;
     }
-    result->result_metadata->Set(ANDROID_SCALER_CROP_REGION, chosen_crop_region,
-                                 ARRAY_SIZE(info.scaler_crop_region_default_));
+    // The camera service splits an application's zoom into the ratio and a residual crop
+    // region, and unscales this result's region by this result's ratio to join them again:
+    // the result states the region this centred camera applies, the requested size centred
+    // in the array (camera_crop.hpp), not the whole array and not the request's origin. The
+    // session layer (ZoomRatioMapper) has divided the request's region by the ratio before
+    // this state sees it and multiplies the result's back, so the ratio is not used here.
+    camera_metadata_ro_entry_t asked;
+    const bool has_asked =
+        request_settings_->Get(ANDROID_SCALER_CROP_REGION, &asked) == OK;
+    const andarium::camera::CropRegion crop = andarium::camera::result_crop_region(
+        has_asked ? asked.data.i32 : nullptr, has_asked ? asked.count : 0,
+        {chosen_crop_region[0], chosen_crop_region[1], chosen_crop_region[2],
+         chosen_crop_region[3]},
+        info.max_zoom_);
+    const int32_t crop_region[4] = {crop.left, crop.top, crop.width, crop.height};
+    result->result_metadata->Set(ANDROID_SCALER_CROP_REGION, crop_region,
+                                 ARRAY_SIZE(crop_region));
     if (info.report_active_sensor_crop_) {
       int32_t active_crop_region[4];
       // width
